{
  "$comment": "Free-tier providers and the models maava AI offers. Free tiers change often: check each provider's limits and terms before relying on them. Providers with a keyEnv are used only when that key is set; keyless providers (OVHcloud, Kilo Code, LLM7) work out of the box, so the router answers with no keys at all. Keyless limits are per IP, so every member shares them. Limits are per key; the router keeps under them and fails over when a provider says no. dataUse: 'no-training' (the provider says prompts aren't used for training), 'may-train' (free-tier prompts may be used to train or improve models), or 'unknown'. terms: 'ok' (the provider's terms plainly allow serving people through it) or 'caution' (read them before relying on it; ratings follow OmniRoute's ToS table). freeTier: the published free allowance, shown on /v1/budget; tpd: tokens a day per model or pool. Aliases list routes in tiers (a nested list is one tier): tiers are tried in order and the alias's strategy (priority, round-robin, least-used, headroom) orders the routes within a tier. Checked 2026-11-09 against https://github.com/mnfst/awesome-free-llm-apis.",
  "providers": {
    "groq": {
      "name": "Groq",
      "baseUrl": "https://api.groq.com/openai/v1",
      "keyEnv": "GROQ_API_KEY",
      "dataUse": "unknown",
      "terms": "caution",
      "freeTier": {
        "note": "Free plan: limits per model, about 200,000 tokens a day each.",
        "source": "https://console.groq.com/docs/rate-limits"
      },
      "models": {
        "openai/gpt-oss-120b": {
          "context": 131072,
          "rpm": 30,
          "rpd": 1000,
          "tpd": 200000
        },
        "openai/gpt-oss-20b": {
          "context": 131072,
          "rpm": 30,
          "rpd": 1000,
          "tpd": 200000
        },
        "qwen/qwen3.8-27b": {
          "context": 131072,
          "rpm": 30,
          "rpd": 1000,
          "tpd": 200000
        }
      }
    },
